   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "When a man lives heedlessly,"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "craving grows in them like a camel’s foot creeper."
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "They jump from one thing to the next, like a langur"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "greedy for fruit in a forest grove."
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "Whoever is beaten by this wretched craving,"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "this attachment to the world,"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "their sorrow grows,"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "like grass in the rain."
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "But whoever prevails over this wretched craving,"
    },
    {
     "n": 10,
     "text": "so hard to get over in the world,"
    },
    {
     "n": 11,
     "text": "their sorrows fall from them,"
    },
    {
     "n": 12,
     "text": "like a drop from a lotus-leaf."
    },
    {
     "n": 13,
     "text": "I say this to you, good people,"
    },
    {
     "n": 14,
     "text": "all those who have gathered here:"
    },
    {
     "n": 15,
     "text": "dig up the root of craving,"
    },
    {
     "n": 16,
     "text": "as you’d dig up grass in search of roots."
    },
    {
     "n": 17,
     "text": "Don’t let Māra break you again and again,"
    },
    {
     "n": 18,
     "text": "like a stream breaking a reed."
    },
    {
     "n": 19,
     "text": "A tree grows back even when cut down,"
    },
    {
     "n": 20,
     "text": "so long as its roots are strong and undamaged;"
    },
    {
     "n": 21,
     "text": "suffering springs up again and again,"
    },
    {
     "n": 22,
     "text": "so long as the tendency to craving is not pulled out."
    },
    {
     "n": 23,
     "text": "A person of low views"
    },
    {
     "n": 24,
     "text": "in whom the thirty-six streams"
    },
    {
     "n": 25,
     "text": "that flow to pleasure are mighty,"
    },
    {
     "n": 26,
     "text": "is swept away by lustful thoughts."
    },
    {
     "n": 27,
     "text": "The streams flow everywhere;"
    },
    {
     "n": 28,
     "text": "a weed springs up and remains."
    },
    {
     "n": 29,
     "text": "Seeing this weed that has been born,"
    },
    {
     "n": 30,
     "text": "cut the root with wisdom."
    },
    {
     "n": 31,
     "text": "A personage’s joys"
    },
    {
     "n": 32,
     "text": "flow from senses and cravings."
    },
    {
     "n": 33,
     "text": "Seekers of happiness, bent on pleasure,"
    },
    {
     "n": 34,
     "text": "continue to be reborn and grow old."
    },
    {
     "n": 35,
     "text": "People governed by thirst,"
    },
    {
     "n": 36,
     "text": "crawl about like a trapped rabbit."
    },
    {
     "n": 37,
     "text": "Bound and fettered, for a long time"
    },
    {
     "n": 38,
     "text": "they return to pain time and again."
    },
    {
     "n": 39,
     "text": "People governed by thirst,"
    },
    {
     "n": 40,
     "text": "crawl about like a trapped rabbit."
    },
    {
     "n": 41,
     "text": "That’s why one who longs for dispassion"
    },
    {
     "n": 42,
     "text": "should dispel thirst."
    },
    {
     "n": 43,
     "text": "Unsnarled, they set out for the jungle,"
    },
    {
     "n": 44,
     "text": "then they run right back to the jungle they left behind."
    },
    {
     "n": 45,
     "text": "Just look at this individual!"
    },
    {
     "n": 46,
     "text": "Freed, they run to bondage."
    },
    {
     "n": 47,
     "text": "The attentive say that shackle is not strong"
    },
    {
     "n": 48,
     "text": "that’s made of iron, wood, or knots."
    },
    {
     "n": 49,
     "text": "But obsession with jeweled earrings,"
    },
    {
     "n": 50,
     "text": "concern for your partners and children:"
    },
    {
     "n": 51,
     "text": "this, say the attentive, is a strong shackle"
    },
    {
     "n": 52,
     "text": "dragging the indulgent down, hard to escape."
    },
    {
     "n": 53,
     "text": "Having cut this one too they go forth,"
    },
    {
     "n": 54,
     "text": "unconcerned, having given up sensual pleasures."
    },
    {
     "n": 55,
     "text": "Besotted by lust they fall into the stream,"
    },
    {
     "n": 56,
     "text": "like a spider caught in the web she wove."
    },
    {
     "n": 57,
     "text": "The attentive proceed, having cut this one too,"
    },
    {
     "n": 58,
     "text": "unconcerned, having given up all suffering."
    },
    {
     "n": 59,
     "text": "Let go of the past, let go of the future,"
    },
    {
     "n": 60,
     "text": "let go of the present, having gone beyond rebirth."
    },
    {
     "n": 61,
     "text": "With your heart freed in every respect,"
    },
    {
     "n": 62,
     "text": "you’ll not come again to rebirth and old age."
    },
    {
     "n": 63,
     "text": "For a personage churned by thoughts,"
    },
    {
     "n": 64,
     "text": "very lustful, focusing on beauty,"
    },
    {
     "n": 65,
     "text": "their craving grows and grows,"
    },
    {
     "n": 66,
     "text": "tying them with a stout bond."
    },
    {
     "n": 67,
     "text": "But one who loves to calm their thoughts,"
    },
    {
     "n": 68,
     "text": "developing perception of ugliness, ever mindful,"
    },
    {
     "n": 69,
     "text": "will surely eliminate that craving,"
    },
    {
     "n": 70,
     "text": "cutting off the bonds of Māra."
    },
    {
     "n": 71,
     "text": "One who is confident, unafraid,"
    },
    {
     "n": 72,
     "text": "rid of craving, free of blemish,"
    },
    {
     "n": 73,
     "text": "having struck down the arrows flying to future lives,"
    },
    {
     "n": 74,
     "text": "this bag of bones is their last."
    },
    {
     "n": 75,
     "text": "Rid of craving, free of grasping,"
    },
    {
     "n": 76,
     "text": "expert in the definition of terms,"
    },
    {
     "n": 77,
     "text": "knowing the correct"
    },
    {
     "n": 78,
     "text": "structure and sequence of syllables,"
    },
    {
     "n": 79,
     "text": "they are said to be one who bears their final body,"
    },
    {
     "n": 80,
     "text": "one of great wisdom, a great person."
    },
    {
     "n": 81,
     "text": "I am the vanquisher of all, the knower of all,"
    },
    {
     "n": 82,
     "text": "unsullied in the midst of all things."
    },
    {
     "n": 83,
     "text": "I’ve given up all, freed in the ending of craving."
    },
    {
     "n": 84,
     "text": "Since I know for myself, whose follower should I be?"
    },
    {
     "n": 85,
     "text": "The gift of the teaching surmounts all other gifts;"
    },
    {
     "n": 86,
     "text": "the taste of the teaching surmounts all other tastes;"
    },
    {
     "n": 87,
     "text": "the joy of the teaching surmounts all other joys;"
    },
    {
     "n": 88,
     "text": "the ending of craving surmounts all suffering."
    },
    {
     "n": 89,
     "text": "Riches ruin a simpleton,"
    },
    {
     "n": 90,
     "text": "but not a seeker of the far shore."
    },
    {
     "n": 91,
     "text": "From craving for wealth, a simpleton"
    },
    {
     "n": 92,
     "text": "ruins themselves and others."
    },
    {
     "n": 93,
     "text": "Weeds are the bane of crops,"
    },
    {
     "n": 94,
     "text": "but greed is these folk’s bane."
    },
    {
     "n": 95,
     "text": "That’s why a gift to one rid of greed"
    },
    {
     "n": 96,
     "text": "is so very fruitful."
    },
    {
     "n": 97,
     "text": "Weeds are the bane of crops,"
    },
    {
     "n": 98,
     "text": "but hate is these folk’s bane."
    },
    {
     "n": 99,
     "text": "That’s why a gift to one rid of hate"
    },
    {
     "n": 100,
     "text": "is so very fruitful."
    },
    {
     "n": 101,
     "text": "Weeds are the bane of crops,"
    },
    {
     "n": 102,
     "text": "but delusion is these folk’s bane."
    },
    {
     "n": 103,
     "text": "That’s why a gift to one rid of delusion"
    },
    {
     "n": 104,
     "text": "is so very fruitful."
    },
    {
     "n": 105,
     "text": "Weeds are the bane of crops,"
    },
    {
     "n": 106,
     "text": "but desire is these folk’s bane."
    },
    {
     "n": 107,
     "text": "That’s why a gift to one rid of desire"
    },
    {
     "n": 108,
     "text": "is so very fruitful."
